TEXT 232 -800 Left 5 ;400kV/120kV Yy0 Dreischenkelkern (Three legs core) vs Dy5 Dreischenkelkern\nunsymmetrische Last NOTE: See the sum of the three secondary voltages (displacement\nof the transformer starpoint)
TEXT 504 -208 Left 2 ;Three limbs core
TEXT 872 -208 Left 2 ;Three limbs core
TEXT 392 72 Left 2 ;Because of the high displacement of the starpoint voltage \nwith the Yy0 and the tree leg core\nthe starpoint of a Yy0 transformer can only burdened by 10%\nNOTE: If the starpoint of the high voltage side is also grounded\nthe displacement is much lower
TEXT 776 80 Left 2 ;Because of the lower displacement of the starpoint voltage\nthe starpoint of a Dy5 transformer can be burdened by 100%
TEXT 320 -208 Left 2 ;Instead of the Yy0 with three leg core \nsee also 3x1 core and five leg core\nIn this case the starpoint is very volatile\nSee also 9limbs with DAW (tertiary delta) \nHere the starpoint is as stable as with Dy5
TEXT 600 -208 Left 2 ;I think that the cettleflow magnetic\nresistance is about 1e5
